  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1966-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "In base \\(2,\\) the left exponent is \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(6x+3)+2(3x+6)\\\\ &\\qquad=12x+15, \\end{aligned} \\] and the right exponent is \\(3(4x+5)=12x+15.\\) The equation is an identity for every real \\(x,\\) so it has more than three real solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite every term with base \\(2\\)",
        "Compare the total exponent on each side before trying to solve for \\(x\\)"
      ],
